Subject: [PATCH 059/230] Add opt-in banner ad slots behind ADGRAM_ENABLED
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Task card only covers in-Telegram placements, so there was no passive
banner surface on either screen. AdBanner owns the container (React renders no
script tags) and injects the provider code from an effect, with a marked TODO
for the snippet; it returns null unless ADGRAM_ENABLED is exactly "true", and
renders nothing until the SDK is ready so a blocked or hung load can never
leave a hollow sponsored frame in the feed. vite.config maps the un-prefixed
name into the bundle because Vite only inlines VITE_-prefixed vars on its own.

